.TH RADVD 8 2026-09-25 "Substrate" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
radvd \- minimal IPv6 router advertisement sender
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B radvd
.I interface
.IR prefix [/ length ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B radvd
sends an unsolicited ICMPv6 Router Advertisement on
.I interface
every 60 seconds, so that hosts on the link can configure a global address
by stateless autoconfiguration and use this host as their default router.
It has no configuration file and no options, never answers Router
Solicitations, and runs in the foreground until it is killed or a send fails.
.PP
.I prefix
is an IPv6 address in the form accepted by
.BR inet_pton (3);
.I length
is the prefix length, 64 if omitted.
Bits of
.I prefix
beyond
.I length
are cleared before it is advertised.
.PP
Each advertisement is built by hand and sent over an
.B AF_PACKET
socket to the all-nodes group ff02::1 (Ethernet 33:33:00:00:00:01), with
hop limit 255.
Its source address is the IPv6 address the kernel reports for the interface
with the
.B SIOCGIFADDR_IN6
ioctl.
It carries:
.IP \(bu 2
current hop limit 64, the M and O flags clear, router lifetime 1800 seconds,
reachable time and retransmission timer 0 (unspecified);
.IP \(bu 2
a source link-layer address option with the interface's MAC address;
.IP \(bu 2
one prefix information option for
.IR prefix / length ,
with the on-link (L) and autonomous (A) flags set and valid and preferred
lifetimes of 10000 seconds.
.PP
A line naming the interface, its index and the prefix is printed to
standard output at startup.
.B radvd
is not started by any of the boot scripts.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
A send failed; the error is reported on standard error.
.TP
.B 1
Too few arguments, an invalid prefix, or the interface's hardware address,
index or IPv6 address could not be read, or the packet socket could not be
created.
.SH EXAMPLE
Advertise the site prefix fec0::/64 on eth0:
.EX
# radvd eth0 fec0::/64 &
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ifconfig (8),
.BR dhclient (8),
.BR init (8)
.SH STANDARDS
Sends Router Advertisement messages as described in RFC 4861 (Neighbor
Discovery for IPv6), for use with RFC 4862 stateless address
autoconfiguration.
.SH BUGS
The prefix length is not checked: it should be between 0 and 128.
.PP
The source address is whatever
.B SIOCGIFADDR_IN6
returns for the interface, which RFC 4861 requires to be link-local but
is not checked.
